-- title:
--   Freeness and fibrewise rank of B[[x]]/(ρ)
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative noetherian local ring, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $\rho\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be an $n$-tuple of multivariate power series, each with vanishing constant coefficient. Assume that there is an $N$ such that $X_i^N$ lies in the ideal $I$ generated by the range of $\rho$ for every variable index $i$, and that the quotient ring $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]/I$ is a finite $B$-module. The conclusion is twofold: first, $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]/I$ is a free $B$-module; second, for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f\colon B \to \kappa$, the $\kappa$-dimension of $\kappa[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ modulo the ideal generated by the coefficientwise images $\mathrm{map}\,f\,(\rho_i)$ equals the $B$-rank (`Module.finrank`) of $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]/I$. Thus the rank of the quotient is insensitive to the choice of field-valued specialisation of $B$, including specialisations not factoring through the residue field.
--
--   This is the local freeness-and-constant-degree statement underlying the notion of a finite locally free kernel of prescribed degree for formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: it converts module-finiteness of a quotient of a power series ring by a system of $n$ series with nilpotent coordinates into freeness together with a degree that is the same on all fibres. It is used in the treatment of kernels of degree $d$ over fields, in the finiteness and projectivity of kernel algebras, and in the comparison of ranks along maps with small kernel.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_free_quotient_and_finrank_quotient_map_eq_of_finite_of_isLocalRing.lean

